-- title:
--   A place is centred at at most one good point
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the field $k_A$ is its residue field.
--
--   **Base data.** A prime $q$ with $5\le q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $k_A$ together with `hW`, which says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: those places $w$ that are rational (the map $k_A\to$ residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ on the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q k_A`, the set of $j$ such that every elliptic curve over $k_A$ with invariant $j$ has no nonzero point annihilated by $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of intermediate fields of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; the first is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-field generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb Q$, the second the analogous base change of the function field of level $q^2M'$ with group `levelH q M'`, the kernel of `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')` on $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$. Write $F=$ `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   **Constant reduction.** A term `R₀ : ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`, that is: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` whose intersection with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC k_A M'` with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with reduction along $A\to k_A$, the property that every nonzero element becomes, after scaling by a constant, an integer with nonzero residue, and a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with orders of elements through `Finsupp.mapDomain`. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $k_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Igusa components.** An index $ζ$ in `Idx q`, a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), the projective line over $\mathbb Z/q$; and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by $W$. Four hypotheses govern $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$: `hIg_inf` describes the ring at `lineInfty q` (the point $[1:0]$) as a Gauss ring, $f\in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`; `hIg` says every line $\ell$ is of the form `redQ q γ • lineInfty q` for some $γ\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` says $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; `hIg_perm` says that for every index $ζ'$ and every $γ\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the operation of taking preimages under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ along some permutation of the projective line.
--
--   **Supersingular rings.** `hSS_A`: for $s\in W$ and $x\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ in $F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ if and only if $x\in A$. `hSS_over`: for $s\in W$ and $f\in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has nonnegative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of the rational $q$-expansion `jq` has nonnegative order, and such that the `R₀`-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, one has: the image of $f$ in $F$ under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue in $k_A$ equals the value of $s$ at the residue of $f$, the difference of that image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal. `hSS_fix`: each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is its own preimage under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $ζ'$ and all $γ\in\Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr`: for each $s\in W$ there is $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that for every $a\in A$ the element $t-a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   **Prolongation.** A term `R : RegularProlongation A (fieldBar q M') (xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M'))`, i.e. a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$ cutting out $A$ on constants, with a surjective residue map onto the level-$q^2M'$ function field over $k_A$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with reduction on $A$ and satisfying the scaling condition; `hR : R.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)`; and `hR₀O`, which says that an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when its image in $F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** An element $π\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $π^{q^2-1}=q$ and $π\in A$. A subfield $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $π_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $π_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`), has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$ (`hκ`). A prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $ζ_0\in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $ϖ_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $ϖ_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ with $x\in A_1$ iff $x\in A$ (`hA₁`), $A_1$ being a discrete valuation ring and henselian.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Give $F$ its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F$ over $k_0$ satisfying: (a) the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $F$; (b) $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all indices $ζ'$ and all $γ\in\Gamma_0(M')$; (c) for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to F$ with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$; (d) $F_0$ contains every $f\in F$ whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`;
--
--   and, writing $T_1$ for the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $K_1$, for every $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map agrees with the inclusion of $K_1$ into $F$ on elements of $A_1$, and every $j_1\in T_1$ whose image in $F$ is the inclusion of the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion `jq`, with $j_1\ne 0$:
--
--   Consider the scheme $\mathfrak X_1=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}=\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ and $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}=\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, with canonical morphisms $ι_{\mathrm{Fin}},ι_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ and structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A_1$. Four predicates are introduced. For $x\in\mathfrak X_1$ and $f\in T_1$, `InStalk x f` holds when for every prime $y$ of the first chart algebra with $ι_{\mathrm{Fin}}$-image $x$ there are $g,h$ in that algebra with $h\notin y$ and $f\,h=g$, and likewise for every prime of the second chart algebra with $ι_{\mathrm{Inf}}$-image $x$; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g\in y$ in both clauses. For a place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` holds when $P$ is rational and, for every $f\in T_1$ with `InStalk x f`, the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$, the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ lies in $A$, and the valuation of that value is $<1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. Finally `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of five clauses: the `toBase`-image of $x$ is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}A_1$; every $y$ with $x\rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$; for every prime $y$ of the first chart algebra with $ι_{\mathrm{Fin}}$-image $x$, every element of that algebra whose image in $F$ is a nonunit of `R.integers` lies in $y$; the same for the second chart algebra and $ι_{\mathrm{Inf}}$; and for every prime $y$ of the first chart algebra with $ι_{\mathrm{Fin}}$-image $x$, every algebraically closed field $Ω$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $φ$ from that algebra to $Ω$ with kernel $y$, the element $φ(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ does not lie in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7).
--
--   The assertion is: for all $x,x'\in\mathfrak X_1$ with `GoodPt x` and `GoodPt x'`, and every place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `Centred P x` and `Centred P x'`, one has $x=x'$.
--
--   A separatedness statement for the two-chart integral model of the full-level function field: a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-rational place of $F$ can be centred at no more than one good point of the special fibre, so that the residue discs attached to distinct good points are disjoint. It is used in the construction of the smooth Igusa base model, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks), where the discs $\{P : P \text{ centred at } x\}$ serve as the residue discs of the model.
